final.exact_config:
Deploy BOTH layers on EVERY node (3-5). The after-sb-* values MUST be identical cluster-wide or the connection is hard-refused at the P_PROTOCOL handshake (drbd_receiver.c:5625-5638, "incompatible after-sb-Npri settings" -> CS_HARD disconnect -> StandAlone). Put these in the resource template for BOTH the arbiter "cluster" resource and every VM-disk resource.

resource <name> {
  net {
    after-sb-0pri discard-zero-changes;   # both-Secondary heal: zero-write loser -> SYNC_TARGET_USE_BITMAP (incremental)
    after-sb-1pri discard-secondary;      # covers the window where ex-Primary is still R_PRIMARY at handshake
    after-sb-2pri disconnect;             # a genuine dual-WRITE two-primary brain MUST hard-stop (no silent loss)
    rr-conflict disconnect;
  }
  options {
    quorum majority;                                 # LINBIT standard; "all" also valid for 3-node
    on-no-quorum suspend-io;                          # freeze (NOT io-error) so guest FS does not error out
    on-suspended-primary-outdated force-secondary;   # demote ex-Primary on the outdate/reconnect leg
  }
  handlers {
    fence-peer  "/usr/lib/bedrock/bedrock-fence-peer";
    # optional: after-resync-target / split-brain "/usr/lib/bedrock/bedrock-sb-notify";
  }
}

# global / resource-level (LAYER 2):
resource <name> {
  net { fencing resource-only; }   # resource-only, NOT resource-and-stonith — bedrock-d owns reboot/STONITH
}

LAYER 1 (after-sb) is the operative lever for the OBSERVED scenario B and is SUFFICIENT for the v1.0 goal on its own. LAYER 2 (bedrock-d self-outdates the minority loser via `drbdadm outdate <res>`, optionally driven by the fence-peer handler reading the witness verdict) is the cleaner belt-and-suspenders that makes the heal a near-zero-resync RULE_LOST_QUORUM reintegration. drbdadm/auto-promote must stay OFF (bedrock-d is sole promote authority).

IMPORTANT FRAMING CORRECTION (from verification): SPLIT_BRAIN_AUTO_RECOVER does NOT auto-heal by itself — its descriptor has .disconnect=true (drbd_receiver.c:209-211). It merely ROUTES into drbd_asb_recover_{0,1,2}p. With the DEFAULT after-sb=ASB_DISCONNECT (drbd_limits.h:158-160) those functions hit `case ASB_DISCONNECT: break` and return SPLIT_BRAIN_DISCONNECT -> "dropping connection" -> StandAlone. The after-sb config above is what converts the SAME AUTO_RECOVER case into an incremental SYNC_TARGET_USE_BITMAP resync. So the config is not optional polish — it is THE fix.

